config RING
	bool "ring: a byte FIFO between two contexts"
	default y
	depends on COMPILER_ATOMICS
	select STATUS
	select IO
	help
	  el_ring: a first-in, first-out buffer of bytes over caller-provided
	  storage, filled by one context while another empties it, with no
	  lock: an interrupt handler and a thread, or two threads. Its two
	  sides are also an el_writer and an el_reader. Freestanding: needs
	  only memcpy(). Needs a compiler that turns a load and a store of an
	  atomic word into instructions (docs/adr/0023); CMake probes that
	  the two compile.

config RING_ZEPHYR_UART
	bool "ring_zephyr_uart: a Zephyr UART's receive interrupt filling a ring"
	default y
	depends on RING && PLATFORM_ZEPHYR_UART_IRQ
	help
	  el_zephyr_uart_irq: a UART's receive interrupt writes what arrives
	  into a ring the caller set up, counts what did not fit, and calls
	  the application when bytes arrive, so that a thread can wait for
	  them and read them through the ring's reader. For a sensor or a
	  modem on a UART whose bytes must not be lost while the thread is
	  busy. Available in a Zephyr build whose configuration has
	  CONFIG_SERIAL and CONFIG_UART_INTERRUPT_DRIVEN.
